PAYLOAD HANDLING CONTRACT (MUST FOLLOW)
- Client uses JWT in header: Authorization: Bearer <token>
- Encrypted inbound payload is always JSON: { "data": "<encrypted payload>" }
- EndpointPolicy controls payload handling:
  - If endpoint expects ENCRYPTED: pass-through, do NOT touch body.
  - If endpoint expects DECRYPTED/PLAIN: decrypt inbound "data" and forward plaintext body.

CRYPTO: CONFIGURABLE PER SERVICE/ENDPOINT
- Algorithm MUST be configurable per Service (default) and overridable per Endpoint:
  - Supported algorithms: "AES_256_GCM", "AES_256_CBC_HMAC", "NONE"
- CryptoConfig fields:
  - Algorithm
  - KeySource (UserProfileKey | ServiceKey | EndpointKey)
  - Encoding (Base64/Hex)
  - RequireIv (true/false)
  - IvSource (UserProfileIv | ServiceIv | EndpointIv)
  - PayloadWrapperFieldName (always "data")
- Keys/IV per user profile are stored in DB; service-level defaults also stored in DB.
- The gateway must resolve the effective crypto config in this order:
  Endpoint override -> Service default -> Global default

AUTHORIZATION (MUST ENFORCE BEFORE PROXY)
- Validate JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry.
- Resolve Client/User identity from JWT claim (e.g., "sub" or "client_id").
- Ensure the JWT (and client) is permitted to call the specific Product/Service/Endpoint:
  - Allowlist in DB: client -> endpoint permissions
  - Required scopes/claims per endpoint
- If not allowed: 403 (never forward).

DATA STORES / INFRA
- PostgreSQL: source of truth for Product/Service/Endpoint registry, policies, clients, keys/IV, permissions.
- ValKey (Redis-compatible): caching + fast policy/user lookups to reduce DB hits in hot path.
- Kafka: optional event emission for audit/telemetry/business events when enabled by policy (event-driven support).

PERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS (VERY IMPORTANT)
- Very low latency:
  - Cache policy resolution in ValKey with TTL + local in-memory cache (IMemoryCache) if safe.
  - Precompile lookups to dictionaries (keyed by routeId or endpointId).
  - Avoid per-request DB calls; only fall back when cache miss.
  - Minimal allocations, no LINQ in hot path, System.Text.Json source-generated contexts if appropriate.
  - Use pooled buffers for decrypt/encrypt transforms with size caps.

YARP REQUIREMENTS
- Use YARP Routes/Clusters for proxying; dynamically build routes from DB registry at startup and refresh periodically (background refresh) OR support hot reload using a config provider.
- Use custom transforms:
  - DecryptTransform (only when endpoint expects plaintext)
  - PassThroughTransform (no-op)
- Support load balancing, health checks, per-route timeouts.

OBSERVABILITY
- OpenTelemetry tracing + metrics with route/service/endpoint tags.
- Correlation ID.
- Structured logs with PII-safe redaction (never log decrypted payload or secrets).

